{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdPpyWDxajjHphANG3Gzq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about a ROS2 (Robot Operating System 2) problem. They have a subscriber to `/camera/image_raw` that never receives messages, even though `ros2 topic hz` shows the topic is publishing at 30 Hz. The code compiles and the node starts, so there's no obvious compile-time or startup issue.\n\nThis is a classic ROS2 troubleshooting question. Let me think about common causes:\n\n1. **Quality of Service (QoS) mismatch** - This is the most common issue in ROS2. The publisher and subscriber need compatible QoS settings. Common mismatches:\n   - Publisher uses reliable delivery, subscriber uses best-effort\n   - Publisher uses transient_local durability, subscriber uses volatile\n   - History depth mismatch\n   - Lease duration issues\n\n2. **Callback not being called** - The message might be being received but the callback isn't being invoked because:\n   - The executor isn't running/spinning\n   - The node isn't being added to the executor properly\n   - The callback is blocking or throwing an exception\n\n3. **Wrong message type** - The subscriber is expecting a different message type than what's being published\n\n4. **Node lifecycle** - The node might not be in the right state\n\n5. **Namespace issues** - Although `ros2 topic hz` works, so the topic is accessible\n\nThe most likely culprit is QoS mismatch, especially in ROS2 where QoS settings are more strict than ROS1.\n\nSince this is a ROS2 perception/robotics question, I should use the ros2-perception skill to help provide better guidance. Actually, looking at the skill again, it's about \"image_transport, cv_bridge, vision_msgs, depth_image_proc, laser_geometry, pcl_ros\" - these are libraries, not really a troubleshooting guide.\n\nLet me provide practical troubleshooting steps for this common issue. I should ask to see 